`/Users/tam/Desktop/DNA-OS-INFRASTRUCTURE/connections/email-alert-source/contract.ts` is the entire public surface — 20 lines, re-exports only:

```ts
export { fetchAlertEmails } from "./adapter";
export { EmailSourceError } from "./types";
export type { EmailSourceConfig, EmailSourceErrorCode, FetchAlertEmailsResult,
              UpstreamAlertMessage, UpstreamResponse } from "./types";
```

`host-runtime.ts` is intentionally **not** re-exported (`contract.ts:7-8`): "`httpPostJson` stays private so no caller can point this adapter at an arbitrary host." Consumers import from `../contract` (see `tests/adapter.test.ts:19`), never from `adapter.ts` directly.

Schemas, all in `/Users/tam/Desktop/DNA-OS-INFRASTRUCTURE/connections/email-alert-source/types.ts` (plain TS interfaces — no JSON Schema, no Zod):

- `EmailSourceConfig` — line 28: `endpoint_url`, `secret_header_name`, `secret_value`, `timeout_ms?` (default 20s at `adapter.ts:86`).
- `UpstreamAlertMessage` — line 48: `id`, `threadId`, `internalDate?`, `date?`, `from?`, `subject?`, `bodyText?`. Mirrors the existing gmail-client output so upstream needn't invent a shape.
- `UpstreamResponse` — line 59: `{ ok?, messages?, error? }`.
- `EmailSourceErrorCode` — line 65: `NOT_CONFIGURED | UNAUTHORIZED | UPSTREAM_ERROR | UNREACHABLE | MALFORMED_RESPONSE`.
- `EmailSourceError extends Error` — line 72.
- **`FetchAlertEmailsResult` — line 87**, the output contract:
  ```ts
  readonly ok: boolean;
  readonly emails: readonly { message_id; thread_id; sender;
                              received_at; subject; body }[];
  readonly error_code: EmailSourceErrorCode | null;
  readonly detail: string;
  readonly source_endpoint: string;   // provenance
  readonly fetched_at: string;
  ```
  Contract guarantee (lines 82-86): always returned, never thrown; `emails` is empty whenever `ok` is false — "there is no partial-success shape that could be mistaken for 'no alerts today'."

The `emails` element type is already `control/alert-correlation/`'s `RawAlertEmail` input shape — the join is by structural typing, not a shared imported type. (I could not read `control/alert-correlation/contract.ts`; it's outside my sandbox and returned EPERM.)

