{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XceviZJ2mNizR9nT8T5VxM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# connections/email-alert-source/\n2\t\n3\t**หน้าที่:** the EMAIL INPUT ADAPTER between the **existing** Gmail reader\n4\tand `control/alert-correlation/`. It reads no mail. It performs one\n5\tauthenticated HTTP call and translates field names.\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\tEXISTING GMAIL READER  (dna-os-deadboard/supabase/functions/_shared/gmail-client.ts, Deno)\n9\t        ↓  HTTP + shared secret\n10\tEMAIL INPUT ADAPTER    (this folder, Node)\n11\t        ↓  RawAlertEmail[]\n12\tcontrol/alert-correlation/\n13\t        ↓\n14\tincident pipeline\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\t## The existing reader this reuses\n18\t\n19\t| | |\n20\t|---|---|\n21\t| Source path | `~/Desktop/dna-os-deadboard/supabase/functions/_shared/gmail-client.ts` (99 lines) |\n22\t| Exports | `getGmailAccessToken`, `searchGmailMessageIds`, `fetchGmailMessage`, `extractBodyText`, `getSubjectHeader` |\n23\t| Scope | `gmail.readonly` — never send/modify/delete |\n24\t| Runtime owner | Supabase Edge Functions (Deno), project `vibrant-hawking` |\n25\t| Credential boundary | `GMAIL_CLIENT_ID` / `GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET` / `GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN` in the Edge Function's own env. **Never copied into DNA OS.** |\n26\t| Already used by | `bank-email-sync` (pg_cron **every 5 min**, production), `subscription-email-sync`, `supabase-billing-sync`, `system-health-check` |\n27\t\n28\t`subscription-email-sync` already keeps a provider table of deterministic\n29\t`from:` fragments (Google, OpenAI, Anthropic, RunPod, Vercel, GitHub,\n30\tApple, Hostinger) — the same closed, sender-scoped style this adapter\n31\trequires. The async worker pattern the Owner asked for already exists and\n32\talready runs.\n33\t\n34\t## CREDENTIAL BOUNDARY — unchanged by this folder\n35\t\n36\tDNA OS gains **no** Google credential. `credentials/registry/` still holds\n37\tonly `github` and `railway`. The OAuth refresh token stays where it is,\n38\tinside the Edge Function environment, and this adapter authenticates to\n39\tthe *function* with a per-function shared secret supplied by its caller —\n40\tthe same `x-<function>-secret` header pattern the existing functions use.\n41\t\n42\t## What is enforced, not just promised\n43\t\n44\t`./tests/adapter.test.ts` scans the **code** of every file here (comments\n45\tstripped, because these files deliberately document what they do *not*\n46\tdo) for `oauth2.googleapis`, `gmail.googleapis`, `users.messages`,\n47\t`refresh_token`, `GMAIL_CLIENT`, `nodemailer`, `imapflow`, `imap`.\n48\tMutation-verified: adding a real `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`\n49\tconstant makes A1 fail; removing it makes it pass.\n50\t\n51\tAlso enforced:\n52\t- an unscoped query (`\"\"`, `is:unread`) is **refused** — a query must\n53\t  start with `from:` / `subject:` / `newer_than:` / `{`\n54\t- a missing endpoint or secret fails **NOT_CONFIGURED** with zero emails\n55\t- an unreachable reader fails **UNREACHABLE** — there is no\n56\t  read-Gmail-directly fallback, by design\n57\t- a message with no parseable date is **rejected**, never stamped `now`\n58\t  (that would corrupt alert-correlation's claim-vs-observation timing)\n59\t\n60\t## NOT_YET_BUILT — the upstream endpoint\n61\t\n62\tThis adapter is complete and tested, but **nothing is deployed for it to\n63\tcall yet**. The existing Edge Functions read mail for *bank*,\n64\t*subscription* and *billing* purposes and return their own domain records\n65\t— none returns raw provider-alert messages, and Railway is not in\n66\t`subscription-email-sync`'s provider table.\n67\t\n68\tClosing that needs a small sibling function in **dna-os-deadboard** that\n69\timports the same `_shared/gmail-client.ts` and returns\n70\t`{ ok, messages: [{ id, threadId, internalDate, from, subject, bodyText }] }`.\n71\tThat is an extension of the existing capability at its proper boundary —\n72\t**not** a new reader.\n73\t\n74\tIt was deliberately **not** written by this task: it means writing into a\n75\tproduction repo that handles real bank and payment data, and deploying to\n76\ta live Supabase project. That needs the Owner's explicit go-ahead, not an\n77\tinference from \"connect email alerts\".\n78\t\n79\tUntil it exists, `fetchAlertEmails` returns `NOT_CONFIGURED` honestly, and\n80\t`control/alert-correlation/` can still be driven from any other source of\n81\t`RawAlertEmail` records.\n82\t\n83\t## Verification\n84\t\n85\t```\n86\tnpx tsc --noEmit                                                   # clean\n87\tnpx tsx connections/email-alert-source/tests/adapter.test.ts       # 11 passed, 0 failed  (needs Node >=18)\n88\t```\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23f64995-c361-420b-a9fb-4a7994c65c73","uuid":"a0a3f48e-07b8-4b1c-bb06-7108569ab00b","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:16:58.499Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tam/Desktop/DNA-OS-INFRASTRUCTURE/connections/email-alert-source/README.md","content":"# connections/email-alert-source/\n\n**หน้าที่:** the EMAIL INPUT ADAPTER between the **existing** Gmail reader\nand `control/alert-correlation/`. It reads no mail. It performs one\nauthenticated HTTP call and translates field names.\n\n```\nEXISTING GMAIL READER  (dna-os-deadboard/supabase/functions/_shared/gmail-client.ts, Deno)\n        ↓  HTTP + shared secret\nEMAIL INPUT ADAPTER    (this folder, Node)\n        ↓  RawAlertEmail[]\ncontrol/alert-correlation/\n        ↓\nincident pipeline\n```\n\n## The existing reader this reuses\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Source path | `~/Desktop/dna-os-deadboard/supabase/functions/_shared/gmail-client.ts` (99 lines) |\n| Exports | `getGmailAccessToken`, `searchGmailMessageIds`, `fetchGmailMessage`, `extractBodyText`, `getSubjectHeader` |\n| Scope | `gmail.readonly` — never send/modify/delete |\n| Runtime owner | Supabase Edge Functions (Deno), project `vibrant-hawking` |\n| Credential boundary | `GMAIL_CLIENT_ID` / `GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET` / `GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN` in the Edge Function's own env. **Never copied into DNA OS.** |\n| Already used by | `bank-email-sync` (pg_cron **every 5 min**, production), `subscription-email-sync`, `supabase-billing-sync`, `system-health-check` |\n\n`subscription-email-sync` already keeps a provider table of deterministic\n`from:` fragments (Google, OpenAI, Anthropic, RunPod, Vercel, GitHub,\nApple, Hostinger) — the same closed, sender-scoped style this adapter\nrequires. The async worker pattern the Owner asked for already exists and\nalready runs.\n\n## CREDENTIAL BOUNDARY — unchanged by this folder\n\nDNA OS gains **no** Google credential. `credentials/registry/` still holds\nonly `github` and `railway`. The OAuth refresh token stays where it is,\ninside the Edge Function environment, and this adapter authenticates to\nthe *function* with a per-function shared secret supplied by its caller —\nthe same `x-<function>-secret` header pattern the existing functions use.\n\n## What is enforced, not just promised\n\n`./tests/adapter.test.ts` scans the **code** of every file here (comments\nstripped, because these files deliberately document what they do *not*\ndo) for `oauth2.googleapis`, `gmail.googleapis`, `users.messages`,\n`refresh_token`, `GMAIL_CLIENT`, `nodemailer`, `imapflow`, `imap`.\nMutation-verified: adding a real `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`\nconstant makes A1 fail; removing it makes it pass.\n\nAlso enforced:\n- an unscoped query (`\"\"`, `is:unread`) is **refused** — a query must\n  start with `from:` / `subject:` / `newer_than:` / `{`\n- a missing endpoint or secret fails **NOT_CONFIGURED** with zero emails\n- an unreachable reader fails **UNREACHABLE** — there is no\n  read-Gmail-directly fallback, by design\n- a message with no parseable date is **rejected**, never stamped `now`\n  (that would corrupt alert-correlation's claim-vs-observation timing)\n\n## NOT_YET_BUILT — the upstream endpoint\n\nThis adapter is complete and tested, but **nothing is deployed for it to\ncall yet**. The existing Edge Functions read mail for *bank*,\n*subscription* and *billing* purposes and return their own domain records\n— none returns raw provider-alert messages, and Railway is not in\n`subscription-email-sync`'s provider table.\n\nClosing that needs a small sibling function in **dna-os-deadboard** that\nimports the same `_shared/gmail-client.ts` and returns\n`{ ok, messages: [{ id, threadId, internalDate, from, subject, bodyText }] }`.\nThat is an extension of the existing capability at its proper boundary —\n**not** a new reader.\n\nIt was deliberately **not** written by this task: it means writing into a\nproduction repo that handles real bank and payment data, and deploying to\na live Supabase project. That needs the Owner's explicit go-ahead, not an\ninference from \"connect email alerts\".\n\nUntil it exists, `fetchAlertEmails` returns `NOT_CONFIGURED` honestly, and\n`control/alert-correlation/` can still be driven from any other source of\n`RawAlertEmail` records.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nnpx tsc --noEmit                                                   # clean\nnpx tsx connections/email-alert-source/tests/adapter.test.ts       # 11 passed, 0 failed  (needs Node >=18)\n```\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
